window.docContents[228].resolve({"/The-Proved-Spine/Kind-of-property-and-kind-of-quantity-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-6___-13_RPAR_/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Kind-of-property-and-kind-of-quantity-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-6___-13_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\nA kind-of-property (§6.19) bundles a terminological id, a scale (from the scale types), and an optional examination principle. A kind\nis a kind-of-quantity (§13.3.1) iff its scale has magnitude (is at least\nordinal).\n\nA structure with DecidableEq. IsQuantity, and the scale divisions\nIsNominal/IsOrdinal/IsDifferential/IsRational (§13.2), are definitional\npredicates over the scale field.\n\nA nominal kind is, by construction, not a kind-of-quantity: it has no\nmagnitude. Uses kind-of-property.\n\nUnfold IsQuantity, IsNominal, and HasMagnitude; the scale is nominal, so\nscale ≠ nominal is false.\n\nA rational kind is a kind-of-quantity. Uses kind-of-property.\n\nThe scale is ratio, so scale ≠ nominal holds; unfold and simplify.\n\nA kind is a ratio quantity (VIM4 2CD 1.3) when its scale is ratio: the\noperators  are defined, so its quantities have an absolute zero and\nform ratios.\n\nIsRational k := k.scale = .ratio.\n\nA kind is an interval quantity (VIM4 2CD 1.4) when its scale is interval: the\noperators  are defined (differences are meaningful), but ratios are not.\n\nIsDifferential k := k.scale = .interval.\n\nA kind is an ordinal quantity (VIM4 2CD 1.33) when its scale is ordinal: only\nthe order  is defined, with neither differences nor ratios.\n\nIsOrdinal k := k.scale = .ordinal.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009The Proved Spine","header":"5.2. Kind-of-property and kind-of-quantity (Dybkær Ch. 6, 13)","id":"/The-Proved-Spine/Kind-of-property-and-kind-of-quantity-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-6___-13_RPAR_/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Kind-of-property-and-kind-of-quantity-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-6___-13_RPAR_"}});